<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Sukkalmah dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">1970 BCE – 1500 BCE (approx.) · capital Susa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The long-lived dynasty of 'grand regents' that ruled Elam from Susa for nearly five centuries, at its height a great power in Hammurabi's world.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 1970 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebarat-ii">Ebarat</a> (Eparti), possibly the last of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/shimashki-dynasty">Shimashki</a> kings, founded a new royal line in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a>. His successors took the title <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sukkalmah">sukkalmah</a>, 'grand regent', a term borrowed from Sumerian administration, and ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa">Susa</a> over lowland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khuzestan">Khuzestan</a> and the highlands of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-anshan">Anshan</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Power was shared in a distinctive system: the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sukkalmah">sukkalmah</a> ruled as overlord, a '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sukkal">sukkal</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimashki-dynasty">Shimashki</a>' acted as his deputy, and a 'sukkal of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa">Susa</a>' governed the city, with succession often passing between brothers and nephews claimed as 'sons of the sister'. Susa produced legal contracts in Akkadian alongside Elamite cults of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inshushinak">Inshushinak</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humban">Humban</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siwe-palar-khuppak">Siwe-palar-huppak</a>, in the 1760s BCE, Elam intervened deep in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>, took <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/eshnunna">Eshnunna</a> and was courted by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mari">Mari</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>A coalition led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammurabi">Hammurabi of Babylon</a> drove the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamites">Elamites</a> back in 1764 BCE. The dynasty survived, but sources thin out after the 17th century BCE, and by about 1500 BCE it gave way to the kings of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/middle-elamite-kingdom">Middle Elamite kingdom</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sukkalmah-dynasty.jpg" alt="Sukkalmah dynasty" width="320" height="231"><figcaption>Image: Enyavar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_Near_East_1600BC.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1970 BCE – 1500 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century-bce">20th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century-bce">16th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Susa</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ebarat, Siwe-palar-huppak, Kutir-Nahhunte I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Elamite religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Elamite, Akkadian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Epartid dynasty, Sukkalmah</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1735&amp;focus=sukkalmah-dynasty" aria-label="Sukkalmah dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5921 1007 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sukkalmah dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6241 1263L6241 1263M6241 1263L6241 1263M6241 1263L6241 1263"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6241 1263h0M6241 1263h0M6241 1263h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6241 1263h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6241 1263h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Susa. <a href="/atlas?year=-1735&amp;focus=sukkalmah-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
